 class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hundred#English\" title=\"hundred\">hundred</a></span>, <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/thousand#English\" title=\"thousand\">thousand</a></span>, <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/million#English\" title=\"million\">million</a></span>, etc.</span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt215\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used in some phrases denoting quantity, such as <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_few#English\" title=\"a few\">a few</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_good_many#English\" title=\"a good many\">a good many</a></i>, a <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/couple#English\" title=\"couple\">couple</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_little#English\" title=\"a little\">a little</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_bit#English\" title=\"a bit\">a bit</a></i>, etc.</span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt221\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used before a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/numeral#Noun\" title=\"numeral\">numeral</a>.</span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt226\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used in some adverbial phrases denoting the degree or extent of an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/action#Noun\" title=\"action\">action</a>, such as <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_little#English\" title=\"a little\">a little</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_bit#English\" title=\"a bit\">a bit</a></i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/a_lot#English\" title=\"a lot\">a lot</a></i>, etc.</span>"},{"definition":"The same; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/one_and_the_same\" title=\"one and the same\">one and the same</a>. <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt231\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used in phrases such as <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/of_a_kind#English\" title=\"of a kind\">of a kind</a></span>, <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/birds_of_a_feather#English\" title=\"birds of a feather\">birds of a feather</a></span>, etc.</span>"},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/any#Determiner\" title=\"any\">Any</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/every#Determiner\" title=\"every\">every</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt234\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">used before a noun which has become modified to limit its scope.</span>"},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/any#Determiner\" title=\"any\">Any</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt238\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">used with a negative to indicate not a single one.</span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt245\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used before an adjective that modifies a noun (singular or plural) delimited by a numeral.</span>"},{"definition":"One; someone named; <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt248\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">used before a person's name, suggesting that the speaker knows little about the person other than the name.</span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt251\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Used before an adjective modifying a person's name, typically used to emphasize that person's current condition or emotional state.</span>"},{"definition":"Someone or something like; similar to; <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt255\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">used before a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/proper_noun#Noun\" title=\"proper noun\">proper noun</a> to create an example out of it</span>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Preposition","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<i>To do with separation;</i> In, into. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt273\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<i>To do with time;</i> Each, per, in, on, by. <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt277\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Often occurs between two nouns, where the first noun occurs at the end of a verbal phrase.</span> <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt278\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<i>To do with status;</i> In. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt284\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt288\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <i>To do with position or direction;</i> In, on, at, by, towards, onto. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt289\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt293\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <i>To do with process, with a passive verb;</i> In the course of, experiencing. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt294\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt298\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <i>To do with an action, an active verb;</i> Engaged in. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt299\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt304\" typeof=\"mw